# {{ name }} — generated by `knext create`.
#
# Ships under the name `gitignore.hbs`, not `.gitignore.hbs`: npm's packer
# strips any file literally named `.gitignore` from a published tarball
# (along with `.npmignore`, `.git`, and a handful of other VCS names) no
# matter what `files` says, so a template shipped under that exact name would
# silently vanish from `@getknext/core` on publish and this file would never
# reach a scaffolded app. `knext create` renders this template and writes it
# out as `.gitignore` in the app root.
#
# Covers both `--builder default` (standalone) and `--builder vinext` scratch
# output — one shared file rather than a builder-specific pair, since an
# unused pattern here is harmless and the alternative is two nearly-identical
# files to keep in sync.

# ── Secrets and local credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The runtime reads config from Kubernetes Secrets via env (see
# `.claude/rules/security.md` in this repo, or your own platform's
# equivalent), never from a file in the image — nothing here is needed to
# build or deploy. Committing one of these is a credential leak, not just
# clutter.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
.npmrc
.netrc
kubeconfig
.kube/

# ── Dependencies and build output ────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
.next
.output
.vinext
dist
build
*.tsbuildinfo

# Compiled single-executables — ~60-90 MB each, and build OUTPUT: `kn-next
# build` (or `bun build --compile`) regenerates them. Two different binary
# basenames, one per build target (the standalone target's is NOT a prefix of
# the vinext target's, so both patterns are needed).
knext-exec*
knext-standalone-exec*
server

# ── Test, coverage and editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────
coverage
.nyc_output
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
